E.129.100 - The system shall support enabling and configuring the Source Data Verification external module (monitor, data entry and data manager roles; SDV action tag regex; ignore action tag; re-verification trigger), shall reject invalid configurations, and shall record every configuration change to the module's View Logs page.
E.129.200 - The system shall allow monitors to mark fields as requiring SDV, verify and unverify individual fields, raise monitor queries that data entry users respond to (and data managers when permitted), accept, re-raise or close those queries, and mark forms as SDV complete or SDV not required (with a reason) only when all required fields are verified and no queries are open. A change to a verified value shall remove its verification and, depending on the configured trigger, return a completed form to 'Re-verification required'. Every SDV action shall be recorded in the project Logging.
E.129.300 - The system shall provide an SDV dashboard listing form SDV status, monitor queries and progress by site, with filtering, paging and CSV export, restricted to the user's data access group, and an SDV plan page on which only monitors can change which fields require SDV.
